description:
LIFECYCLE EVENT BUS (P2): Current events.rs has EventType enum with 13 variants (AgentRegistered/Started/Progress/Blocked/Completed/Failed/Crashed/Stopped/Replaced/HandoffCreated/PromptStalled/Rejected + WorkSubmitted/Verified/Accepted/Rejected/ReviewEscalated). Need comprehensive lifecycle events.

NEW EVENT TYPES:
- PeerSpawned { peer_id, pid, workspace, disposition }
- PeerReady { peer_id }
- PeerCrashed { peer_id, exit_code, signal, workspace_lease_id }
- PeerStopped { peer_id, reason }
- TaskReceived { task_id, assigned_to }
- TaskExecuting { task_id, peer_id }
- TaskCompleted { task_id, peer_id }
- TaskFailed { task_id, peer_id, error }
- VerificationStarted { task_id, profile }
- VerificationPassed { task_id, evidence_id }
- VerificationFailed { task_id, findings }
- WorkspaceAcquired { lease_id, path, holder }
- WorkspaceReleased { lease_id }
- WorkspaceCleaned { lease_id }
- LeadHandoff { from_lead, to_lead, reason }

EVENT BUS ARCHITECTURE:
- EventBus struct with handlers: HashMap<EventType, Vec<Box<dyn Handler>>>
- emit(event) → dispatch to all registered handlers
- Handler trait: fn handle(&self, event: &Event) -> Result<()>
- RecoveryHandler: on PeerCrashed → cleanup workspace
- EvidenceHandler: on VerificationPassed → persist EvidenceRecord
- NotificationHandler: on events → log to SQLite + optional webhook

FILES:
- crates/anti-core/src/events.rs — expand EventType enum
- crates/anti-daemon/src/bus.rs (NEW) — EventBus, Handler trait, built-in handlers

INTEGRATION:
- Replace direct emit_event() calls with EventBus.emit()
- Register handlers at daemon startup
- Recovery handler wired to TreehouseAdapter

Tests:
- emit PeerCrashed → RecoveryHandler called
- emit VerificationPassed → EvidenceHandler called
- emit without handler → no panic (log warning)

## Context
Phase 3 of PLAN-v3-runtime-engine. Currently the daemon manages peers through Store (SQLite) and HashMap<String, Child> directly, with spawn logic split across spawn/spawn_peer/spawn_peer_impl in main.rs. This bead refactors into a proper PeerManager.

## What to build
Create `crates/anti-daemon/src/peer_manager.rs`:

```rust
pub struct PeerManager {
    store: Arc<Mutex<Store>>,
    children: Arc<Mutex<HashMap<String, Child>>>,
    treehouse: TreehouseAdapter,
}

impl PeerManager {
    /// Phase 1: Validate + persist metadata (with lock)
    pub fn spawn(&self, spec: SpawnSpec) -> Result<PeerHandle, SpawnError>;

    /// Phase 2: Acquire workspace lease (no lock)
    pub fn acquire_workspace(&self, id: &str, repo: &str) -> Result<WorkspaceLease>;

    /// Phase 3: Spawn harness process (no lock)
    pub fn spawn_process(&self, spec: &SpawnSpec, workspace: &WorkspaceLease) -> Result<Child>;

    /// Phase 4: Commit results (with lock)
    pub fn commit_spawn(&self, id: &str, pid: u32, lease: WorkspaceLease) -> Result<()>;

    pub fn stop(&self, id: &str, force: bool) -> Result<()>;
    pub fn wait(&self, id: &str) -> Result<ExitStatus>;
    pub fn terminate(&self, id: &str) -> Result<()>;  // SIGTERM → wait → SIGKILL
}
```

## Critical: Lock discipline
Phase 0 established: NO external I/O under store Mutex. The spawn flow is already split into phases — PeerManager must preserve this:
- Phases with lock: validate, persist, commit
- Phases without lock: treehouse acquire, process spawn

## Reap integration
The existing reap_children background thread (5s poll, try_lock) stays in main.rs but delegates to PeerManager for crash detection → cleanup → event emission.

## Files
- NEW: `crates/anti-daemon/src/peer_manager.rs`
- MODIFY: `crates/anti-daemon/src/main.rs` (use PeerManager, remove duplicated spawn logic)
